    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d722">

                <pb facs="0870" n="768" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg768"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.672/540: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-01-19T19:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 19,
                                1927—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:47 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>8. Department’s No. 10, January 18, 7 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>(1)</label>
                    <item>Since the action of the United States Senate is advisory, am I authorized
                        to intimate to the Government of Turkey that the President of the United
                        States has not rejected the Lausanne Treaty and thereby persuade the
                        Government of Turkey to withhold consideration of the above treaty by the
                        Grand National Assembly?</item>
                    <label>(2)</label>
                    <item>Also, can I suggest the possibility of the treaty being resubmitted at the
                        next session of the Congress for consideration, and cite as precedents the
                        delay in ratification of the Isle of Pines treaty<anchor n="7"
                            xml:id="d722-f1"/> and the Colombian treaty?<anchor n="8"
                            xml:id="d722-f2"/></item>
                    <label/>
                    <item>Any means to gain time for the consideration of the whole question will be
                        very helpful. I leave for Angora on the 20th with Patterson.</item>
                    <label>(3)</label>
                    <item>In order that I may be prepared to meet all questions of the Government of
                        Turkey, could the Department inform me as to the <pb facs="0871" n="769"
                            xml:id="pg769"/> procedure for the resumption of diplomatic relations?
                        Would a Chargé d’Affaires or an Ambassador be sent? May I recall to the
                        attention of the Department that Turkey has not entered into diplomatic
                        relations with other countries until after the exchange of ratifications of
                        treaties of amity has taken place.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
